-- title:
--   First Drinfeld section is the origin on the Gauss branch
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ the symbol $A_0$ abbreviates `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring $A\cap k_0$ of $k_0$; $\kappa_A$ denotes `ResidueField A`.
--
--   *Numerical data.* A prime $q$ and a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓg12`) and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (`hℓgM'`).
--
--   *The big valuation subring and its constant reduction.* A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in `A.nonunits`; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` (the subfield of `LaurentSeries κ_A` generated over $\kappa_A$ by `jqModC κ_A` and `jqNModC κ_A M'`) over $\kappa_A$, which by `hW` is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ_A` of places $w$ satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ_A w`, together with a distinguished element $s \in W$; the inclusion `hle` of intermediate fields $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, that is, the field generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ inside `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`; a constant reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M')` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source field, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with $A$, with orders of functions and with divisor push-forward; the ten clauses of the structure are summarised here); and the hypothesis `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   *The field of small constants.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ (`hπ`), and the hypotheses that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Roots of unity, level group, and the level field.* An element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$; a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; an intermediate field $K$ of `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` over $k_0$ which by `hK` is `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`, the field generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of the $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ function field over $\mathbb Q$, with $K$ an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$; and an element $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq`, the image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, with $j \neq 0$.
--
--   *Functoriality data for the rigid datum.* Three hypotheses asserting stability under Weierstrass variable changes, uniformly in $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` implies `IsGamma1Point (C • W) ℓg (D.variableChange C)`; `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`; and `hL`, that $h \mid \mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,W\,\ell_g\,n\,x$ implies `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` divides $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,(C\bullet W)\,\ell_g\,n\,(u^{-2}(x-r))$. Further, a family of group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras which is chord-tangent (`h𝒢`) and whose identity is the origin section (`h𝒢O`), a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ and $q$ which is a section transport (`h𝒯`), and the two existence hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO`: for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and variable change $C$ there is a graded ring homomorphism `projModelGradingCR W →+*ᵍ projModelGradingCR (C • W)` whose image contains the irrelevant ideal of the target and which `IsVariableChangeHom`, and likewise, for an $A_0$-algebra map $f : T \to T'$, one into `projModelGradingCR (W.map f)` which `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $\mathcal R$ for `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass datum whose level structure over an $A_0$-algebra consists of a $\Gamma_0$-power kernel polynomial for each prime factor of $M'$, a `LevelPData` recording a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, and a raw Drinfeld pair of $q$-level sections, subject to the linking condition.
--
--   *The moduli package and the pinned Tate point.* A package $P_0$ of type `LevelModuliPackageAbs A₀ 𝓡.toLevelModuliDatum`, i.e. an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a point `P₀.univ` over it such that every point of the datum over an $A_0$-algebra is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism; a point $x_0$ of the datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant, read in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, is `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` (`hx₀`); an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism `clC` from $B_0$ to the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` which, after composition with the inclusion into $K$, is the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀` (`hclC`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ to the Tate curve: there are a variable change $C$ over `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and a raw representative $r$ of the datum over $K$ with $\mathrm{Quot.mk}\,r = x_0$, such that, writing $(x_\zeta,y_\zeta) = \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,k_0\,q\,(\xi^q)$ for the toric point attached to the unit $\xi^q$ (a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity): the unit of $C$ satisfies $u\,(2x_\zeta + 1/6) = 2y_\zeta + x_\zeta$ and $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ (constant Hahn series); $r$'s curve, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,q$; for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the coefficientwise image under $f$ of the $p$-component `r.level.1 p` is the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, along $C$ mapped by $f$ and in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`, of $\prod_{a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,(\zeta^a))_1)$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component `r.level.2.1`, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, is the variable change by $C$ of the `LevelPData` $(x_\zeta, y_\zeta, x_\zeta, y_\zeta)$; and there exist $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y \in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of the variable change by $C$ of $\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,q\,(\xi^{\ell_g})\,(1,0)\,(0,-1)$, with the two Drinfeld sections of `r.level.2.2` passing through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   *Residue compatibility.* A ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the residue field of $A_0$ to $\kappa_A$ with $\theta$ carrying the residue of $a \in A_0$ to the residue in $A$ of the image of $a$ (`hθ`).
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every field $\Omega$ which is an algebra over $\kappa_A$, every place $V$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$ (a proper valuation subring of $\Omega$ containing the image of $\kappa_A$ and a principal ideal ring), every ring homomorphism $\rho$ from `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` to $\mathcal O_V = V.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ given by the Gauss presentation `hW₀`, namely $f \in W_0$ if and only if there are power series $x,y$ over $A_0$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and $f \cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $k_0$, such that `hker` holds: for all $h$ in the chart algebra, $\rho(h) = 0$ in $\Omega$ if and only if $h$, viewed in $K$, lies in `W₀.nonunits`; then, for every $A_0$-algebra structure on $\mathcal O_V$, every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\rho_A : B_0 \to \mathcal O_V$ with $\rho_A = \rho \circ \mathrm{clC}$ (`hρA`), and every raw representative $x_V$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathcal O_V$ whose class is the image of `P₀.univ` under $\rho_A$ (`hxV`), there exists a ring homomorphism $\chi_P$ from `OriginChartRing (xV.level.2.2.curve)` — the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the graded ring of the projective model at the coordinate $y$ — to $\Omega$ such that:
--
--   (i) the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\Omega \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_V$ induced by the structure map followed by the first Drinfeld section $(x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P).1$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\chi_P$ followed by the origin-chart immersion `originChartι (xV.level.2.2.curve)`;
--
--   (ii) $\chi_P(\mathrm{xOverY}) = 0$;
--
--   (iii) $\chi_P(\mathrm{zOverY}) = 0$.
--
--   Thus on the Gauss branch the first level section of the specialised universal datum factors through the origin chart and meets it at the origin.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ form of the statement that, at the Tate point of the modular curve $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over the Gauss valuation branch of the chart algebra, the first of the two Drinfeld $q$-level sections specialises to the origin of the Weierstrass model. It is used in the analysis of the semistable model of the modular curve above $q$, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_ringHom_chartAlgFin_residue_eq_originChart_levelAut_of_forall_nsmul_eq_zero_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_ringHom_chartAlgFin_residue_eq_originChart_levelAut_of_forall_nsmul_eq_zero_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1).
